{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>הכרת תכרת</b> — in gematria [this equals] 'that the Torah spoke in the language of humans.' It juxtaposed the gatherer to the blasphemer — to teach you that they were in one period, as found in Chullin Chapter 1. And since Sabbath is as severe as idolatry, it juxtaposed to them the passage of tzitzit, which is also weighed against all the commandments, as written: 'and you shall remember all the commandments of HaShem.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:17.054809097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}